        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe logic is placed well \u2014 `findPossibleDuplicate` is a private helper that directly parallels the existing `isIdentityKeyAlreadyUsed`/`findHouseholdMembers`/`countNamesakes` helpers, reuses `normalizeHouseholdKey` for the last-name comparison (matching household matching as advertised), and the call site in `saveOwner` sits naturally alongside the other `owner.isNew()` soft-flag blocks (bulk-signup warning, namesake count). The model/schema/OpenAPI additions mirror the existing advisory fields (`bulkSignupWarning`, `householdMemberCount`) consistently. No catch-all growth, no duplicated concern.\n\nOne concrete idiomatic finding:\n\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.java:344-345` uses inline fully-qualified names `java.util.Objects.equals(...)` and `java.util.Comparator.comparing(...)`. This file consistently imports its `java.util` types (see lines 37-41: `Collection`, `List`, `Set`, `UUID`, `Supplier`), and the rest of the class refers to them by simple name. The inline FQNs break that established convention and read as out of place. Add `import java.util.Objects;` and `import java.util.Comparator;` and use the simple names, matching the surrounding code."
